  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The use hereby permitted shall operate between the hours of 9am -6pm Monday - Friday and 9am-4pm Saturdays only, with no operation on Sundays or bank holidays. \r\rReason: To ensure that there is not an unreasonable impact on neighbour amenity and to accord wit Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The change of use hereby permitted shall only apply to the proposed outbuilding, as shown in the approved drawings 0100 and 0200 and must only be operated by an inhabitant of the main dwelling at 36 Windsor Avenue, North Cheam SM3 9RX.\r\rReason: To allow a change of use of the outbuilding but to ensure that a separate planning unit is not created with no attachment to the main residential dwelling and to ensure that the permitted use remains suitable for the residential area in which it is located in accordance with Policies 10, 28 and 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Planning Fire Safety Strategy prepared by Mr Darren Mead dated 28/07/25.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted, shall only be occupied by a Hair studio falling within Class E (c) (iii) (any other services which it is appropriate to provide in a commercial, business or service locality) as defined by the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987 (as amended), notwithstanding the changes to the Use Classes Order in relation to Use Class E. No other 'E' use class is permitted without seeking full planning permission.\r\rReason: To enable the Local Planning Authority to assess all the implications of the development on highway safety, parking and neighbouring amenities in accordance with Policies 29, 36 and 37 of Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
